Phloem-Tide
Ingredients: DETROIT TECHNO + CHICAGO / CITY / URBAN BLUES + CINEMATIC, EPIC & ORCHESTRAL + Whistle
Creative Catalyst: The genre was born when field botanists calibrated laboratory bio-voltmeters onto tropical greenhouse leaves, routing the plants' live electrical impedance into modular synthesizers to trigger industrial drum machines.

Phloem-Tide sounds like a gale-force collision between midnight factory machinery and smoky South Side taverns: relentless, syncopated four-on-the-floor Roland 909 kicks rumble beneath weeping, overdriven bottleneck slide guitars and crying mouth-blown whistles, all swept upward by towering, cinematic 50-piece string arrangements and erratic synthesizer sweeps modulated by the live bio-electrical resistance of creeping tropical foliage.

